1
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:03,930
Okay...

2
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:07,510
The x-tens are online.

3
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:10,640
Gentlemen, I am now about send a signal

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:13,500
From this laptop through our local isp

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,350
Racing down fiber-optic cable at the speed of light

6
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,660
To san francisco, bouncing off a satellite

7
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,860
In geosynchronous orbit to lisbon, portugal,

8
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:21,990
Where the data packets

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,810
Will be handed off to submerged trans-atlantic cables

10
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:25,800
Terminating in halifax, nova scotia

11
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,180
And transferred across the continent

12
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:29,370
Via microwave relays back to our isp

13
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:31,470
And the x-ten receiver attached to this...

14
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:34,570
Lamp.

15
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:39,280
Look at me. look at me. I've got goose bumps.

16
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,160
Are we ready on the stereo?

17
00:00:41,170 --> 00:00:42,320
Go for stereo.

18
00:01:03,910 --> 00:01:04,710
Hey, guys.

19
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:06,220
Hi. hello. hello.

20
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,150
It's a little loud.

21
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,450
No problem-- turning it down.

22
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:14,220
San francisco, lisbon, halifax...

23
00:01:14,230 --> 00:01:15,820
And voila.

24
00:01:15,830 --> 00:01:16,860
Okay, thanks.

25
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:19,690
Hang on, hang on. do you not realize what we just did?

26
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:22,290
Yeah, you turned your stereo down with you laptop.

27
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,290
No, we turned our stereo down by sending a snall

28
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,860
Around the world via the internet.

29
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:30,150
You know, you can just get one of those universal remotes

30
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,500
At radio shack. they're really cheap.

31
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,520
No, no. You don't get it.

32
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:37,090
Howard, enable public access.

33
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,760
Public access enabled.

34
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,860
Boy, that's terrific. I'll see ya.

35
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,370
No, hang on, hang on.

36
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,930
See?

37
00:01:50,350 --> 00:01:51,840
No.

38
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:54,520
Someone in szechwan province, china

39
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:55,680
is using his computer

40
00:01:55,690 --> 00:01:57,710
To turn our lights on and off.

41
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:00,910
Well, that's handy.

42
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,440
Here is the question. Why?

43
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:07,500
Because we can.

44
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,540
They found the remote-control cars.

45
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,960
Well, wait, wait, what's on top of that?

46
00:02:14,970 --> 00:02:17,520
Wireless web cams. wave hello.

47
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:20,600
The monster truck is out of austin, texas,

48
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:22,490
And the blue viper is being operated

49
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,720
From suburban tel aviv.

50
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:28,780
You may want to put on slacks.

51
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:30,390
What?

52
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,470
Ew, stop it.

53
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,020
No leave me alone

54
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,190
Who's running the red corvette?

55
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,930
That would be me.

56
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,310
The.Cooper.Hofstadter.Polarization

57
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:07,660
You know, in the future

58
00:03:07,670 --> 00:03:09,930
When we're disembodied brains in jars,

59
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,950
We're going to look back at this as eight hours well wasted.

60
00:03:14,510 --> 00:03:15,980
I don't want to be in a jar.

61
00:03:15,990 --> 00:03:18,510
I want my brain in an android body.

62
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:21,660
Eight feet tall and ripped.

63
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:23,410
I'm with you.

64
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:25,540
I just have to make sure that if I'm a synthetic human,

65
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:27,870
I'd still be jewish.

66
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,200
I promised my mother.

67
00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:36,840
I suppose you could have your android penis circumcised,

68
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:38,650
But that's something

69
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:41,090
Your rabbi would have to discuss with the manufacturer.

70
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:44,600
Not to mention you'd have to power down on saturdays.

71
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,970
Sheldon, why is this letter in the trash?

72
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:51,790
Well, there's always the possibility that a trash can

73
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:54,180
Spontaneously formed around the letter,

74
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,230
But occam's razor

75
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,990
Would suggest that someone threw it out.

76
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,050
It's from the institute for experimental physics.

77
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,950
They want us to present our paper

78
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,650
On the properties of supersolids

79
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,480
At the topical conference on bose einstein condensates.

80
00:04:06,490 --> 00:04:08,690
I know, I read it before I threw it out.

81
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:12,450
Okay, if I may drill down to the bedrock of my question

82
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,150
Why did you throw it out?

83
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:16,650
Because I have no interest in standing in the rose room

84
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:17,980
Of the Pasadena Marriott

85
00:04:17,990 --> 00:04:20,320
In front of a group of judgmental strangers

86
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:21,870
Who wouldn't recognize true genius

87
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:24,710
If it was standing in front of them giving a speech.

88
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,380
Which, if I were there, it would be.

89
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,700
I don't know, sheldon.

90
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,910
Those topical conference on bose einstein condensates

91
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:32,740
Parties are legendary.

92
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:34,220
Forget the parties.

93
00:04:34,230 --> 00:04:37,490
Forget the parties? what a nerd.

94
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:40,850
Are there any other honors I've gotten that I don't know about?

95
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:42,290
Did ups drop off a nobel prize

96
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,950
With my name on it?

97
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,590
Leonard, please don't take this the wrong way,

98
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,120
But the day you win a nobel prize

99
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:49,050
Is the day I begin my research

100
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:52,430
On the drag coefficient of tassels on flying carpets.

101
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,720
Ooh, the only thing missing

102
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:57,240
From that insult was "your mama."

103
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,610
I got one.

104
00:04:58,620 --> 00:05:01,220
Hey, leonard, your mama's research methodology is so flawed...

105
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:03,460
Shut up, howard.

106
00:05:03,500 --> 00:05:05,020
Sheldon, we have to do this.

107
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:06,320
No, we don't.

108
00:05:06,330 --> 00:05:08,620
We have to take in nourishment, expel waste,

109
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:11,090
And inhale enough oxygen to keep our cells from dying.

110
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:13,250
Everything else is optional.

111
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:15,890
Okay, let me put it this way, I'm doing it.

112
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:17,850
You can't. I'm the lead author.

113
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:20,290
Come on, the only reason you're the lead author

114
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,020
Is because we went alphabetically.

115
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,820
I let you think we went alphabetically

116
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,220
To spare you the humiliation

117
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:26,790
Of dealing with the fact that it was my idea.

118
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,550
Not to put too fine a point on it,

119
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,450
But I was throwing you a bone.

120
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,420
You're welcome.

121
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:35,750
Excuse me, I designed the experiment that proved the hypothesis.

122
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,730
It doesn't need proving.

123
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:39,820
So the entire scientific community

124
00:05:39,830 --> 00:05:41,250
Is just supposed to take your word?

125
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:44,150
They're not supposed to, but they should.

126
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,020
All right, I don't care what you say,

127
00:05:46,030 --> 00:05:48,220
I'm going to the conference and I'm presenting our findings.

128
00:05:48,230 --> 00:05:50,030
And I forbid it.

129
00:05:51,190 --> 00:05:52,680
You forbid it?

130
00:05:52,690 --> 00:05:55,350
If I'm not taking credit for our work, then nobody is.

131
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,090
So you admit that it's our work? no.

132
00:05:57,100 --> 00:06:00,190
Once again, I'm throwing you a bone.

133
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,860
And once again you are welcome.

134
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:08,500
Oh, no, he didn't

135
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,290
So, how's it going with sheldon?

136
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,250
Are you guys still not talking to each other?

137
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,020
Not only is he still not talking to me,

138
00:06:16,030 --> 00:06:18,220
But there's this thing he does where he stares at you

139
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:20,300
And tries to get your brain to explode.

140
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:25,060
You know, like in the classic sci-fi movie scanners.

141
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:28,470
Like... bzzz...

142
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:30,350
Never mind.

143
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,110
How about this one?

144
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:36,090
It says, I know my physics, but I'm still a fun guy.

145
00:06:37,550 --> 00:06:39,700
Wow, I didn't know they still made corduroy suits.

146
00:06:39,710 --> 00:06:42,320
They don't.That's why I saved this one.

147
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:44,380
Okay, well, let's just see

148
00:06:44,390 --> 00:06:46,270
What else you have.

149
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:48,320
Okay, here, take this...

150
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:52,390
And this, and this, and these...

151
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,220
Is this all stuff you want me to try on?

152
00:06:54,230 --> 00:06:56,230
No, this is stuff I want you to throw out.

153
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,540
Oh. seriously, don't even give them to charity.

154
00:06:58,550 --> 00:07:00,640
You won't be helping anyone.

155
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:03,700
What's this?

156
00:07:03,710 --> 00:07:06,500
That's the bottle city of kandor.

157
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:11,620
You see, kandor was the capital city

158
00:07:11,630 --> 00:07:12,920
Of the planet krypton.

159
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,390
It was miniaturized by brainiac before krypton exploded,

160
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:17,760
And then rescued by superman.

161
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:21,250
Oh. nice.

162
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:24,720
It's a lot cooler when girls aren't looking at it.

163
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:27,080
Here, why don't you put these on

164
00:07:27,090 --> 00:07:28,710
While I find a shirt and a sport coat that match.

165
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,880
Great, I'll be right back.

166
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:30,990
Where are you going? just put 'em on.

167
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,250
Here?

168
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,590
Oh, are you shy?

169
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:35,790
No, I'm not shy.

170
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,050
Don't worry. I won't look.

171
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:39,050
I know you won't look. why would you look?

172
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:40,490
There's nothing to see... well, not nothing...

173
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,290
Sweetie, put the pants on.

174
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,960
Putting 'em on.

175
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:46,320
So, you know, isn't there maybe some way

176
00:07:46,330 --> 00:07:49,750
You and sheldon could compromise on this whole presentation thing?

177
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,040
No, no.

178
00:07:51,050 --> 00:07:52,720
Scientists do not compromise.

179
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:54,650
Our minds are trained to synthesize facts

180
00:07:54,660 --> 00:07:56,320
And come to inarguable conclusions.

181
00:07:56,330 --> 00:08:00,230
Not to mention, sheldon is bat-crap crazy.

182
00:08:02,030 --> 00:08:04,720
What is this?

183
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:06,730
Oh, careful.

184
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,350
That's my original series

185
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:10,130
Battlestar galactica flight suit.

186
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:13,020
Oh, why didn't you wear it on halloween?

187
00:08:13,030 --> 00:08:16,630
Because it's not a costume. it's a flight suit.

188
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:21,200
Okay, all right, moving on.

189
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,550
Oh, wow, a paisley shirt.

190
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:26,130
Uh-huh, it goes with my corduroy suit.

191
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:30,490
If you mean they should end up in the same place, then I agree.

192
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:33,730
Is this your only tie?

193
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:35,320
Technically, yes.

194
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:37,420
But if you'll notice...

195
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:40,330
It's reversible.

196
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:42,850
So it works as two.

197
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:46,690
Oh sweetie, I don't even think it works as one.

198
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:49,420
Is this all your clothes?

199
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:51,890
Yup. everything since the eighth grade.

200
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,190
The... the eighth grade?

201
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,530
My last growth spurt.

202
00:08:57,150 --> 00:08:59,920
Okay, well, I guess we're back to the corduroy suit.

203
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,630
Great. yep.

204
00:09:03,130 --> 00:09:05,620
I said no. put it down.

205
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,260
Hey, sheldon.

206
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,740
Hello, penny.

207
00:09:16,350 --> 00:09:18,080
Get anything good?

208
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:23,380
Just the latest copy of applied particle physics quarterly.

209
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:27,410
Oh, you know, that is so weird that yours came and mine didn't.

210
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,580
It was a joke.

211
00:09:40,470 --> 00:09:41,530
Yep, tip your waitresses.

212
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,550
I'm here all week.

213
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,070
Penny, just to save you from further awkwardness,

214
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,140
Know that I'm perfectly comfortable with the two of us

215
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:49,950
Climbing the stairs in silence.

216
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,170
Oh, yeah, okay, me, too.

217
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:53,070
Zip it, lock it.

218
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,950
Put it in your pocket.

219
00:10:00,810 --> 00:10:01,870
So, you and leonard.

220
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:03,550
Oh, dear god.

221
00:10:04,110 --> 00:10:05,990
A little misunderstanding, huh?

222
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,680
A little misundersta...?

223
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:11,650
Galileo and the pope had a little misunderstanding.

224
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,570
Anyway, I was talking to leonard this morning,

225
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,280
And I think he feels really bad about it.

226
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,670
Well, how do you feel?

227
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:25,630
I don't understand the question.

228
00:10:25,910 --> 00:10:27,870
No, I'm just asking if it's difficult

229
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:30,100
To be fighting with your best friend.

230
00:10:30,110 --> 00:10:33,100
Oh, I hadn't thought about it like that.

231
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:34,300
I wonder if I've been experiencing

232
00:10:34,310 --> 00:10:36,000
Physiological manifestations

233
00:10:36,010 --> 00:10:39,450
of some sort of unconscious emotional turmoil.

234
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:41,250
Wait. what?

235
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,590
I couldn't poop this morning.

236
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,500
Just talk to him.

237
00:10:48,510 --> 00:10:50,930
I'm sure you guys can work this out.

238
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:52,810
It's certainly preferable to my plan.

239
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,070
Which was?

240
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,540
A powerful laxative.

241
00:10:57,670 --> 00:10:59,860
Okay, so you absolutely should talk to him.

242
00:10:59,870 --> 00:11:01,440
Look, I know leonard values you as a friend,

243
00:11:01,450 --> 00:11:03,540
And he told me himself that without your little idea,

244
00:11:03,550 --> 00:11:05,140
There's no way he could have

245
00:11:05,150 --> 00:11:07,110
Come up with this whole experiment thing.

246
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:12,410
Excuse me. "little idea"?

247
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,170
Yeah, I mean, he tried to explain it to me.

248
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:15,200
I didn't really understand it...

249
00:11:15,210 --> 00:11:16,240
Of course, you didn't.

250
00:11:16,250 --> 00:11:18,370
He said, "little idea"?

251
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:21,950
Well, no, not in... not in those words.

252
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,640
In what words then, exactly?

253
00:11:23,650 --> 00:11:25,300
Um, you know, gee, the exact words...

254
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:26,870
It's more the spirit in which...

255
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:27,800
What did he say?

256
00:11:27,810 --> 00:11:29,650
You had a lucky hunch.

257
00:11:30,950 --> 00:11:32,400
Hey, sheldon, I've been thinking.

258
00:11:32,410 --> 00:11:33,440
Instead of arguing about this...

259
00:11:33,450 --> 00:11:36,230
Don't you ever speak to me again.

260
00:11:37,850 --> 00:11:39,680
Wha...?

261
00:11:40,910 --> 00:11:43,140
He...

262
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:57,170
Okay, I'm leaving for the conference.

263
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,660
Have fun presenting my "lucky hunch."

264
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:01,290
Shel, I didn't mean it like that.

265
00:12:01,290 --> 00:12:02,110
Then why did you say it?

266
00:12:02,110 --> 00:12:03,250
I don't know. I wasn't...

267
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:04,720
Were you trying to impress penny?

268
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,670
No, no, not at all. a little bit.

